From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 02:02:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] drm/sun4i: Output YUV and 10-bit colour from the H616
 display engine

The display engine always outputs 8-bit RGB to the HDMI controller,
which rules out YUV output, YUV 4:2:0 modes and deep colour, and with
it 10-bit video and HDR.

Give the engine an output media bus format and YCbCr encoding, carried
in a CRTC state subclass and latched into the engine when the mode is
set, before the TCON, the mixer and the planes are programmed:

- The H616 (DE33) mixer has a formatter after the blender, which
  subsamples to YUV 4:2:0 and outputs 10 bits per component. Program
  it with the clamp values of the vendor driver, and report the
  formats it can produce through a new format_valid engine callback.
  Everything else keeps outputting 8-bit RGB only.
- For YUV output the blender works in YUV, so each channel CSC unit
  converts its plane into limited range YCbCr of the output encoding
  (BT.601, BT.709 or BT.2020), and the background is YUV black. This
  extends the BT.601-only YUV blending of the TV encoder path.
- For YUV 4:2:0 two pixels are sent per TCON cycle, so the TCON TV
  dot clock and horizontal timings are halved.
- The writeback unit converts YUV blender output of any encoding.

Based on the DE3/DE33 HDMI output series by Jernej Skrabec in
LibreELEC, ported to the register shadow of this driver and to the
TV encoder YUV path.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
